Make less -R pass SGR sequences (ESC [ N ; N m) through to the terminal,
taking no columns, instead of stripping them, so that man pages show
bold and underline and git output keeps its colors. A wrapped line
re-emits the SGR state of the rows above it, and each row that used SGR
ends with a reset.

Lines are now measured in columns but stored in bytes, so line buffers
grow as needed rather than being sized by the screen width. UTF-8
continuation bytes take no columns when Unicode is enabled, and 0x9b,
common inside UTF-8 characters, is no longer shown as a control
character. Searches run on a copy of each line without its SGR, so a
match never lands inside one, and highlights end with SGR 27 rather than
a full reset, so that bold, underline and color survive them.

